{
  "_comment": [
    "Photoshop CS6 default keyboard shortcuts.",
    "",
    "This file is DATA, not code (CLAUDE.md §9). Widgets never hard-code a key",
    "combo; they register a command id here and the CommandRegistry binds it.",
    "",
    "'key' uses Qt's portable sequence syntax. 'Ctrl' maps to Command on macOS",
    "automatically, which is exactly the mapping Photoshop uses, so the same",
    "table serves both target platforms.",
    "",
    "'altKeys' is an optional list of extra sequences that fire the same",
    "command. Menus only ever show 'key'. Aliases are needed where one logical",
    "Photoshop shortcut reaches us as several different key events: Ctrl+'+'",
    "is physically Ctrl+Shift+= on a US layout, so Zoom In has to answer to",
    "Ctrl+= and Ctrl+Shift+= as well.",
    "",
    "Users may override any binding by copying this file to the per-user config",
    "directory; see CommandRegistry::userKeymapPath().",
    "",
    "No two commands may share a key. Qt treats a duplicate as an ambiguous",
    "shortcut and fires NEITHER action, so a clash silently kills both. The",
    "registry warns about one at load; docs/REFERENCE.md lists every binding."
  ],

